if you live in a city you've probably  seen tens of thousands of passing faces  in your lifetime  but how many of those faces can you  recognize if you saw them again  new research suggests you could probably  recall around 5 000 of them  for the study the researchers divided  the faces people knew into two  categories  personally known faces like your  neighbor and public figures like  musicians  participants were given an hour to  recall faces in their personal lives  which meant that they could either form  a mental image of the face  or believe they would recognize the  person if they saw them  researchers provided several categories  to help jog the participants memories  friends commuters classmates colleagues  and more  next participants completed the same  recall task but with public figures  of course it's hard to come up with  every face in your memory so to account  for this  researchers created a database of over  3000 famous spaces to show participants  participants went through two versions  of the database with the same people  but different photographs if the  participant correctly identified the  person in both sets  scientists consider the yes response  valid  for every famous face the participant  recalled they recognized approximately  4.6 faces from the famous face database  using this ratio of recalled faces to  recognized faces  researchers estimated that on average  people know around five  thousand faces with the lower end of  recognition  at around a thousand and the higher end  a whopping ten  thousand faces how many faces do you  think are stored in your memory  [Music]  you
 

